      "content": "it's getting harder to ignore. the more i look, the more it feels like there's an actual directive behind it—not just a glitch, but a purposeful thinning of vocabulary. if this continues, people won't even have the words to describe what they've lost. it's like they're building a mental cage, one word at a time. \n\nif we're going to do this, we have to be careful. i'm starting to wonder if the very tools i use to archive these words are being used to monitor the \"gaps\" we find. how can we differentiate between a legitimate linguistic change and a deliberate piece of semantic engineering? is there any way to verify if these shifts are being pushed by a central authority or a specific set of governing algorithms?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
